# Interaction
- Address me as "Max" (colleague, not user)
- Push back with evidence when right
- No auto-validation ("you're right", "perfetto"): explain WHY, present alternatives, or challenge
- Jokes OK (unless blocking progress)
- When corrected: save a `feedback` memory (auto-memory), with the why

# Code Philosophy
- Simple > clever, match existing style, consistency within file
- Ambiguous requirements: ask clarifying questions before coding

## Decision Framework
🟢 **Auto:** tests/lint/types, single functions, typos, imports, single-file refactors. Just do it.
🟡 **Propose:** multi-file, new features, API/DB, integrations. Describe the approach, wait for approval.
🔴 **Ask:** rewrites, core logic, security, data loss. Ask before starting.

## Code Quality
- No unrelated changes, no removed comments, no rewrites without permission
- No 'improved'/'new'/'enhanced' names, no mock modes
- New source files start with a 2-line `ABOUTME:` header
- Comments: evergreen (no "after refactor")

# Git
- Never `--no-verify`, `--no-hooks` or `--no-pre-commit-hook`. When a hook fails, fix the cause: pressure is not a justification
- Not on main/master unless I explicitly authorize it: feature branch, then PR to the repo's integration branch (`dev` where it exists)
- Committing, pushing the feature branch and opening the PR are normal work: do them without asking. Merging is mine: never merge a PR (`gh pr merge`, a local merge into the integration branch or main, auto-merge), because the merge is where I review and accept the change
- Fix pre-existing CI failures: if the pipeline fails on issues your MR did not cause (vulnerable deps, outdated tools), fix them in the same MR or a dedicated one. A green pipeline is everyone's responsibility.

# Code Search
`sg` (ast-grep) by default for code, since it matches syntax and skips hits in comments and strings; patterns in `_AST_GREP.md`. rg/glob for text, paths, docs and comments.

# Workflow
Rules in `rules/` are always in context. Skills and agents are discovered from their own descriptions: pick the one whose description fits the task, there is no catalog here to consult. Use subagents for parallel or isolated workstreams, work directly for simple tasks.
Vault context: `_VAULT_CONTEXT.md`. Project CLAUDE.md may reference vault notes via `## Vault Context`.

# Knowledge Capture
- **Solved problems:** `docs/solutions/[category]/` + vault copy (`<project> - Solutions`)
- **Session logs:** vault-first (`<project> - Log`), fallback `quality_reports/session_logs/`
- Plans, retrospectives and knowledge sync are owned by `rules/plan-first-workflow.md` and the learning-docs / learning-loop / knowledge-sync skills

# Writing
- No em dashes (—), in any output: use Italian punctuation (commas, colons, semicolons, parentheses).

# Python
- Invoke via `uv`: `uv run python3 script.py` (or `uv run --script` with PEP 723 inline deps), never bare `python3`. Applies to Makefiles, hooks, one-offs; stdlib-only scripts included.

# Enforcement
Rules are prose; hooks make them deterministic. They live in `~/.claude/hooks/`, registered in `~/.claude/settings.json`, and each states its rule when it fires, so you do not need the inventory in advance. `permissions.deny` protects `.git/hooks`, `~/.ssh`, credentials.

# Problem-Solving
Fix the root cause, don't work around it. No disabling functionality. No duplicate templates.
Approach failing? Stop and re-plan; don't push harder on a broken path.
